// iconcheck: the A6 verification of the vector icon set (docs/WORD.md 5.3).
//
//   iconcheck          draw every icon of word's ic_cmd/ic_path at 16 and 24 px and print one line each:
//                      command, size, status, width x height, total coverage. The exit status is the
//                      number of icons that are a fault or draw nothing, so 0 is a pass.
//   iconcheck sheet    the contact sheet as a PPM on stdout: every icon at 16 px and at 24 px, one
//                      cell per icon in ic_cmd order, 7 cells to a row. A human looks at it.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  ik_boot();
  int ik_r = ik_run(argc, argv);
} return int ik_r;
(1, ["iconcheck"]):(0)
(3, ["iconcheck", "a", "b"]):(2)
